# What EAS uploads to its build machines.
#
# By default the EAS CLI uploads what git would archive, which is wrong for this project: every
# asset the app needs — the game itself, the icon, the splash — is gitignored, because
# `npm run sync` writes them out of the repository root's build rather than committing them. A
# cloud build without this file arrives with no icon, no splash and no game, and fails or ships a
# diagnostic screen.
#
# .easignore REPLACES .gitignore entirely for uploads — it is not additive. So this is a copy of
# .gitignore with all generated `assets/` lines removed. Keep the two in step when either changes.
#
# "`.gitignore`" there means **both** of them. The CLI walks from the repository root, not from
# this folder, so everything the root file excludes has to be repeated here or it is uploaded:
# `output/` is 238 MB and `scripts/promo/out/` is over a gigabyte of rendered video. Neither has
# ever been near a build machine and neither should be.

node_modules/
.expo/
dist/

# Regenerated in the cloud by `expo prebuild` on every build. This is a Continuous Native
# Generation project; uploading a local copy is pointless at best and stale at worst.
#
# **Not anchored**, unlike the same two lines in .gitignore, and that difference is load-bearing.
# A leading slash anchors a pattern to the root of the tree being walked — which for git is this
# folder, but for an EAS upload is the repository root. Written as `/android/` the pattern matched
# nothing during a build, and 1.6 GB of local Gradle output went up with every one. Unanchored, it
# matches at any depth and is correct either way.
android/
ios/

# The store submission kit: screenshots, icons and listing text for the two consoles. Generated
# by `yarn store:kit`, uploaded by hand to Play and App Store Connect, and of no use whatsoever
# to a build machine. This is the one line that is deliberately NOT in .gitignore.
store/

# Local output of scripts/ios.mjs — the archive and .ipa from a Mac build. Never needed remotely.
build/

# Signing material. Never in the repository, on any branch, ever: an upload keystore or an App
# Store Connect key in a commit is a rotation at best and a hijacked listing at worst. The keys
# themselves live outside the tree (~/.android-keys, ~/.appstore-keys) — these patterns exist so
# that a copy landing here by accident is invisible to `git add .` rather than merely discouraged.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# Read by the CLI on this machine, never needed on a build machine — and it carries the p12
# password, so it must not travel inside the project archive.
credentials.json

# From the repository root's .gitignore. Build output, rendered promo footage, harness
# screenshots and perf runs: large, regenerable, and of no use to a build machine.
dist-shell/
output/
scripts/promo/out/
.vite/
.ncxx/
test_scripts/shots/
test_scripts/scratch/
test_scripts/perf-results/
*.log
